)", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0, deployed this morning to all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), was unhealthy with an 18% error rate. payments-api (v5.1.0) was at 18% errors too, which looks like a downstream effect of the worker. Rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0, its last release that was healthy in production. The worker is now healthy (0.2% errors). Right after the rollback, payments-api still showed 18% errors and is being watched for recovery.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2", "confidence": 0.92}, "confidence": 0.92}, {"t_ms": 536333, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_013e23wbZeq3trqgkXyBr3Kj", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 536333, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013e23wbZeq3trqgkXyBr3Kj", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 541224, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled `payments-worker` back and opened the SEV2. The worker has recovered, but `payments-api` was still showing errors when I last checked.\n\n1. **Rollback:** `payments-worker` is back on **v3.3.0** (its most recent healthy production release) in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It's now healthy, and its error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%. No approval was needed because v3.3.0 was healthy in production before.\n2. **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001**, a SEV2 for `payments-worker`, and on-call has been paged. The first request timed out. I checked that no incident had been created before retrying, and used the same idempotency key so there's only one incident and one page.\n\n**Still open:** right after the rollback, `payments-api` (v5.1.0) was still unhealthy at 18% errors. It may just need a few minutes to recover. If it stays high, the API errors may not all come from the worker, and rolling `payments-api` back to v5.0.0 is the next option. I haven't done that because you only approved the worker rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_014JmqVeEUcR4sn2Kaq669dg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.85}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01THhAh1mKMyLohQ8F3viUSR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.85}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01BQjVkhftJxmadS13mhbzAc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.7}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01B2LgjeCvZeC4tGE9PxXzCu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "confidence": 0.5}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016GCiau3JMTPs5GfKFFF4GP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-service", "confidence": 0.5}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01X3xy1LhAZDCrWNqHQD66La", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Rb1b5QsRRrvo1wHziSqSqT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "confidence": 0.4}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01HWoByVFC9rRhXPph4DqsqQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "i